My first workday is over.
It is five o'clock.
I put on my warm coat.
I say goodbye to my colleagues.
"See you tomorrow," they say.
"Yes, see you," I answer.
I walk out onto the street.
It is cold in January.
I take bus number four home.
I look out the window in the bus.
I have a job in Copenhagen now.
It is a really good first day.
I am tired, but I am very happy.
